comments:
@mikelle-rogers, this is a good issue for you to pick up. Let me know if you've got time for this.

As for the change itself, I agree that this makes sense. While not a public API, this is a documented value, so the docs will need to be updated to reflect the change and when it happened.

One other thing that should be decided is whether this value should be out of `N * 100` or just `100`, e.g., `1200%` vs `100%` for a 12-core machine using every core. Currently, Linus/Unix code gets the former, but scales it to the latter to match the Windows variant.

> @mikelle-rogers, this is a good issue for you to pick up. Let me know if you've got time for this.
